    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. His start against Seth Lugo is bolstered by a significant 16% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup, providing a high floor for power and runs. Following him, **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) present elite profiles; **Jacob Wilson** is particularly well-situated to exploit a matchup against Schultz, benefiting from a high 19% SP skill boost as he continues to drive the top of the lineup. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** (71.40) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.23) provide excellent secondary value, with the latter capitalizing on a strong platoon advantage against W. Warren.\n\nThe rotation decisions remain lean, with **Brayan Rocchio** emerging as our most difficult omission. His 56.28 score was buoyed by a strong SP skill boost against Phillips, but he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace our current starters. We are closely monitoring the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Kyle Tucker** as their lineups are currently pending; however, their projected scores\u2014all north of 63\u2014remain locked assuming their standard roles. We advise keeping a close eye on **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom are facing pitchers with slow deliveries, creating a prime opportunity for them to manufacture the stolen bases we prioritize. Conversely, **Denzer Guzman** remains benched with a sub-40 score, as the combination of a low batting order position and a difficult matchup against Taj Bradley renders him a clear sit to preserve our game caps.",
